{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#lem:two-sheet-bottleneck","","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> be a polynomial and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>U</mi></math></span> a component of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> on which <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> has degree two, with one simple\ncritical point <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. Write <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></math></span>. Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>, then every connected\nsubset <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span> of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>U</mi></math></span> containing its two roots <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math></span> satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msup><mrow><mi>ℋ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:ani-degree-seven-counterexample","<code>ani</code>’s degree-seven example","<p><em> The monic polynomial <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> in\n<a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow.html#eq:ani-f\">(2)</a> has seven distinct\nzeros in the open unit disc. Every connected set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></math></span> containing two of its\nzeros satisfies <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mrow><mi>ℋ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:critical-value-separation","unformalised isolated-value assertion","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> be monic of degree <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> be a simple critical point, and put\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. Fix <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Suppose every other\ncritical point <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Put\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Then two distinct\nroots are joined inside <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> by a curve <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Γ</mi></math></span> satisfying </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>7</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>length</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Γ</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">(</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mspace width=\"-0.167em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:critical-value-thresholds","conditional numerical thresholds","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> be monic of degree <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span> with all roots in the open unit\ndisc. If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> is a simple critical\npoint with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and,\nfor some <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>, every other\ncritical point <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nthen two roots are joined inside <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> by a curve of length\nstrictly below <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></span>. In degree three\nthe branch-centred choice <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>\nalready works with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span> replaced by\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:low-critical-thirteen-twentyfifths","unformalised small-critical-value\nassertion","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> be\nsquarefree and monic of degree <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi></math></span> be its least critical-value modulus.\nIf <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>25</mn></math></span>, then two distinct\nroots are joined inside <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> by a rectifiable curve of\nlength strictly less than <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:scaled-low-critical","scaling of the preceding assertion","<p><em>\nEvery squarefree monic polynomial of degree <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> has two distinct roots joined in\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>13</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> by a curve of\nlength less than </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>13</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> In every\ndegree the length can be chosen less than <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:sextic-spoke","failure of a prescribed radial\nsegment","<p><em> There exist <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for which every zero of </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> lies in the open unit disc, yet the radial segment from\nthe origin to the zero <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span> leaves\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1041-lemniscate-newton-flow#res:trinomial-all-degree","all-degree monic trinomials","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> with every zero in the\nopen unit disc. For any zero <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ζ</mi></math></span>,\nthe entire segment <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span> lies\nin <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. Distinct zeros\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></span> are therefore\njoined by the broken line <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>0</mn><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></span> of length <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mo>+</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> inside the\nopen unit lemniscate.</em></p>"]]}
